1
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
25 years. Hundreds of victims. Justice for none.

2
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Tales of the Grim Sleeper is a crime, documentary
film directed by Nick Broomfield.

3
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
When Lonnie Franklin Jr.

4
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
was arrested in South Central Los Angeles in 2010 as the suspected murderer of a string of young
black women, police hailed it as the culmination of 20 years of investigations.

5
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Four years later documentary filmmaker Nick Broomfield took his camera
to the alleged killer’s neighborhood for another view.

6
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Self, played by Lonnie Franklin Jr..

7
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Lonnie David Franklin Jr.

8
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
(August 30, 1952 – March 28, 2020), better known by the nickname Grim Sleeper, was an American serial killer who was
responsible for at least ten murders and one attempted murder in Los Angeles, California from 1984 to 2007.

9
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
He was also convicted for rape and sexual violence.

10
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Franklin earned his nickname when he appeared to have taken a
14-year break from his crimes, from 1988 to 2002.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
In July 2010, Franklin was arrested as a suspect, and, after
many delays, his trial began in February 2016.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
On May 5, 2016, the jury convicted him of killing
nine women and one teenage girl.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
On June 6, 2016, the jury returned a verdict of guilty, and on August 10, 2016, the Los Angeles
Superior Court sentenced him to death for each of the ten victims named in the verdict.

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
On March 28, 2020, Franklin was found dead in his cell at San Quentin State
Prison though no cause of death was ever publicly revealed.
